sion record: [the api browser-trust boundary Agent Note](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-07-28-api-browser-trust-boundary.md).
+
+## Built-in token auth
+
+`ConnectionConfig.tokenAuth` enables first-party bearer-token admission for every `/api` HTTP request and both WebSocket downlinks. It accepts a list of opaque tokens and optional scopes (`web`, `tui`, `admin`); the default scope is `admin`. Tokens may arrive as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, `x-dsh-access-token`, the `__Host-dsh-access-token` cookie, or the `dsh-access-token` cookie. Missing or invalid tokens receive `401` on HTTP and a rejected upgrade on WebSocket.
+
+A browser login shortcut is available at `GET /api/auth/login?token=<token>`: it validates the token, sets the `dsh-access-token` HttpOnly cookie, and redirects to `/`. `GET /api/auth/logout` clears the cookie.
+
+An `admin`-scoped token also unlocks the privileged method set that otherwise stays loopback-only (`settings.*`, `credentials.*`, `host.pickDirectory`, `host.openPath`, and the agent-preset authoring methods). This is the authentication layer that makes non-loopback `dsh web` deployments safe to operate.
 
